n\n$$\n-4k=8.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\nk=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288440/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288440"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-287975/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9c63cda8-2840-56f2-8271-c21f55da3cae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-287975/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae1df2cf-9566-5004-8ba6-32d65599da18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-287975/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-287975/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-287975" :question/id #uuid "ceb241e1-ab0e-5069-a882-fcb4fcc9530e" :question/math-academy-id "q-287975" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(2p-3)x=5x\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=2p-3,\\,b=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n2p-3=5.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p & =8 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-287975/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-287975"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288583/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8f9d736a-c682-5a3b-834a-cf8f4b6bcfea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288583/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e095caa4-cf23-54b1-b6e5-42a31cc98a69" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288583/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-288583/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288583" :question/id #uuid "1a4d57ff-6bcc-52bd-8911-d563e2cabe8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-288583" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n2tx+(1-m)=6x+4\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ and $m$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $t+m?$\n\n$t+m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $t$ and $m$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n2tx+(1-m)=6x+4\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2t=6.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we get\n\n$$\n1-m=4.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\nm=-3.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $t=3$ and $m=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\nt+m=3+(-3)=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-288583/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288622/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "24804afb-c846-547d-b85e-18b379f9fa84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288622/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "4497ef92-56d2-5e6c-8447-e67ad0a2a6dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288622/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "5a3159c6-3502-5e5b-b14a-190e83c2ad5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288622/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "5e13c442-1e5d-55b3-a899-50ce6ae315ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288622/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "02150bc2-83b1-5cc9-836e-726a68f7422d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288622/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fad43b24-e43d-59fd-8531-592734d1c035" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-288622/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-288622/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-288622/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-288622/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-288622/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-288622/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288622" :question/id #uuid "107e60f6-2335-50ce-b0c8-2a4b9c9873ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-288622" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(m+2)x+5n=7x+15\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ and $n$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $m+n?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $m$ and $n$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(m+2)x+5n=7x+15\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\nm+2=7.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n5n=15.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $n,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $m=5$ and $n=3,$ we have\n\n$$\nm+n=5+3=8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288622/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288622"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288584/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c01c0cec-8be7-558a-b294-c591d8a541d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288584/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cf47335-2ab5-5b4b-a694-689490ef6c09" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288584/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-288584/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288584" :question/id #uuid "458632c2-a121-5956-b70c-1083bf4954df" :question/math-academy-id "q-288584" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+3)x+2t=x+6\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ and $t$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $s+t?$\n\n$s+t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $s$ and $t$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+3)x+2t=x+6\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n-s+3=1.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $s,$ we get\n\n$$\ns=2.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n2t=6.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $s=2$ and $t=3,$ we have\n\n$$\ns+t=2+3=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-288584/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288584"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288627/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "0a7f8a64-2f69-5092-993e-a304984f7948" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288627/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "c6fc743b-33e4-5360-af1c-36857ae316fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288627/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "3f8428fb-81b8-5ac9-90df-fffde296b0d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288627/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "17b39409-8889-5493-b425-a39858693269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288627/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "6fb56e57-0792-5a8f-be57-957098d787fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288627/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3113796c-a9b9-5cca-82d8-e74e254c5944" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-288627/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer-field/choices ["q-288627/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-288627/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-288627/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-288627/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-288627/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288627" :question/id #uuid "35d716e9-efe6-5b38-accd-60b85b179fe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-288627" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{p}{2}x+q=4x+20\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ and $q$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p+q?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $p$ and $q$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{p}{2}x+q=4x+20\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{p}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we get\n\n$$\nq=20.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $p=8$ and $q=20,$ we have\n\n$$\np+q=8+20=28.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288627/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288627"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288623/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "86ba9a51-3dcb-57d4-a109-8860b0b0ffba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288623/selection/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :answer/id #uuid "2cb62a81-7e10-51d1-983d-1fb6361f5d26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288623/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "54211d78-72db-5c19-a472-1cfab206980d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288623/selection/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34" :answer/id #uuid "46dcdda3-7271-593e-85cc-255bbbc6fe1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288623/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "3c0060fb-5925-59c5-912c-22a664f97716" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288623/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "54e67142-eba3-5d1c-bb60-d1124dacdbc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-288623/selection/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34" :answer-field/choices ["q-288623/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-288623/selection/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" "q-288623/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-288623/selection/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34" "q-288623/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288623" :question/id #uuid "bb84cb7f-b888-57b2-be16-cb2f94243f7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-288623" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n2kx+r=9x+6\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ and $r$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $k+r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $k$ and $r$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n2kx+r=9x+6\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2k=9.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\nr=6.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $k=\\frac{9}{2}$ and $r=6,$ we have\n\n$$\nk+r=\\frac{9}{2}+6=\\frac{21}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288623/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288623"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
